TITLE:Small Incidents Spec
H1:M6 · Making it safe: small incidents (Day 8, Calder) <span class="draft">spec for approval</span>
SUB:About once a week, a small incident from the machines: an hour or two on one deck. You make it safe, clean up, then fix the cause. Not a ship-wide event (those are Pillar 6). Step 2, sub-block 24f. Plan Part 2, M6.
NAV:plain=In plain words|three=The three incidents|when=When they happen|day=Day 8|grow=How it grows|b=Builder|save=Save|tests=Tests|ranges=Builds and keys|faq=FAQ

<p class="note"><b>Approved by the lead (2026-10-18, overnight authority).</b></p>
<section id="plain">
  <h2>In plain words</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Three steps, always in this order:</b> <b>make it safe</b> (isolate it: close the right valve or breaker, upstream, picked from what you see), <b>clean up</b> (mop the water, clear the smoke, help someone out), then <b>fix</b> the cause (an ordinary repair).</li>
    <li><b>It's urgent but kind:</b> a toast and the board's top card ("! Burst pipe, Deck 4 junior wing"); crew reroute around it and talk about it; nobody gets hurt; there's no timer. If you're not on shift or don't come, the crew deal with it (more slowly), and you hear about it at dinner.</li>
    <li><b>Never</b> on an event day (Pillar 6), on a tradition evening, at night (except your own two night shifts, Step 5), on a day off, or in your first week.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="three">
  <h2>The three incidents (more can be added later as data)</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><b>A burst pipe</b><span>A corridor floor is wet and crew step round it. <b>Safe:</b> close the line's valve (two or three valves on the nearby panel; the right one is the one upstream of the wet, following the pipe). <b>Clean:</b> mop the puddle (a few holds). <b>Fix:</b> replace the burst joint (one seal from stores, fitted at the burst).</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">Decks 3, 4, 5</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>The lift sticks</b><span>The main lift stops between decks with someone inside, for up to 20 minutes; crew take the ladder (rides are slow). <b>Safe:</b> at the lift machine room on Deck 5, release the brake (a turn). <b>Clean:</b> help them out at the next deck (a short word; they're grateful for days). <b>Fix:</b> service the lift.</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">the lift</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>The galley alarm</b><span>A scorched pan sets off the galley plant's smoke alarm (the galley plant runs the galley's extraction). <b>Safe:</b> reset the alarm at the galley plant's panel (a hold). <b>Clean:</b> clear the air: open the vents and wait a few minutes. <b>Fix:</b> check the hood (look) and service the galley plant. Brennan is embarrassed.</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">Deck 3</span></span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="when">
  <h2>When they happen</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>About one a week</b>, on a workday between 09:00 and 15:30, from Day 8. Which incident, which day and where are worked out from the week (the same every game).</li>
    <li><b>Your first is fixed:</b> Day 8, Monday, about 10:30 (after the Monday briefing), a burst pipe on Deck 4.</li>
    <li>They come from the machines: a burst pipe is more likely where the pipe valves are worn, the galley alarm when the galley plant is, the lift sticking when the lift is.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="day">
  <h2>Day 8, Monday: your first, with Calder</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><time>10:30</time><b>The call</b><span>An urgent toast: "Calder: Burst pipe, junior wing. With me." She meets you at the Works bay door (or comes to find you, the escort's walking).</span></li>
    <li><time>Safe</time><b>She asks, you pick</b><span>At the wet corridor: "Which valve? Follow the pipe." You choose; if you pick a downstream one she says why not, and you try again.</span></li>
    <li><time>Clean</time><b>Mop</b><span>She hands you the mop. Crew step round you; Tomas makes a joke.</span></li>
    <li><time>Fix</time><b>The joint</b><span>Fetch a seal and fit the joint, Calder watching. "Trained: making it safe, with Calder."</span></li>
  </ol>
  <p class="note">Day 8's small new thing is your work uniform (M2); Calder's "Tomorrow, your test job" line after the briefing is unchanged.</p>
</section>

<section id="grow">
  <h2>How it grows</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 1 · Calder there</b><span>Your first.</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">Day 8</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 2 · First on the scene</b><span>From your second: you go alone; Calder arrives for the fix.</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">after 1</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 3 · The crew wait for you</b><span>As a Senior Officer you say it's safe and direct the crew (Step 5), and on your night shifts, incidents at night are yours.</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">Senior Officer</span></span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="note">Afterwards an optional "Why did it burst?" head-scratcher can follow for a clever fix (Officer and later; never during the make-it-safe step).</p>
</section>

<section id="b" class="builder">
  <h2>For the builder (seat M2, sub-block 24f)</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Section</th><th>What</th><th>Owner</th></tr>
    <tr><td>24f (new)</td><td><code>INCIDENTS</code> (data), the week's plan, the three-step job, the Day 8 training, crew handling when you don't come</td><td>M2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>17</td><td>the machine side: an incident's fix is an ordinary job, posted at the clean-up's end: for a burst, a Tier 1 <code>joint</code> job at the burst (one <code>seal</code>, 20 minutes; the deck's <code>valve</code> machines are Tier 2, so they're never the junior's fix: a worn one just gets its service job as usual); for the lift and the alarm, a repair on the lift machine (<code>5-mainlift-1</code>, see below) or <code>3-galleyplant-1</code> (Tier 1), which the incident sets to faulty (cond 40) when it starts; the lift's <code>lift</code> effect ×3 while stuck</td><td>S</td></tr>
    <tr><td>14 / 10 sim</td><td>a <b>wet patch</b> crew walk round (the corridor tiles under the puddle cost more in pathing for crew, never blocked: no plan changes); the <b>stuck person</b> (a crew member whose plan has them riding the lift at the start minute; held in the car, <code>wait</code>, until released or 40 minutes); Brennan by the galley plant for the alarm; crew remarks for a day (<code>simNote('incident')</code>)</td><td>the social engineer (on call for sim items)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>15 / 15b</td><td>the steps: <code>choose</code> (valve), <code>turn</code> (brake), <code>hold</code> with the <code>mop</code> pose, <code>wait</code> (clear the air), <code>look</code> (the hood)</td><td>P</td></tr>
    <tr><td>8b</td><td>a <b>puddle decal</b> (one flat, see-through disc, lifted 1 cm off the floor so it's never coplanar; instanced, shared with M13 leak hunting later) and a <b>smoke wisp</b> (a few instanced soft quads in the galley); at most 3 draw calls, only during an incident on your deck; the <code>mop</code> pose</td><td>M2 itself (no performance seat tonight), checking the draw calls</td></tr>
    <tr><td>DECKS[3], [4], [5]</td><td>per deck: valve places by the corridors (<code>4-valve-1..3</code> on the junior wing's pipe panel, with the pipe order known: <code>valveLine</code> = upstream first), puddle spots (<code>4-wet-1..2</code>), the lift machine room's brake (<code>5-lift-brake</code>), the galley plant's alarm panel (<code>3-galleyplant-alarm</code>, may be its panel place), vents (<code>3-vent-1</code>)</td><td>seat A</td></tr>
    <tr><td>18 events</td><td>reads only: <code>eventsOn(d)</code> for event days and tradition evenings</td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td>content</td><td>the call, Calder's steps, crew remarks, the stuck person's thanks, Brennan</td><td>W</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <div class="lines">INCIDENTS = {
  burst: { decks: [3, 4, 5], weight: n =&gt; 1 + wornness('valve', n),
           safe: { how: 'choose', at: n + '-valve-panel', opts: valves upstream-first, ok: the first upstream of the wet },
           clean: { how: 'hold', at: n + '-wet-1', mins: 6, pose: 'mop', reps: 3 },
           fix: { job: 'joint', part: 'seal', at: n + '-wet-1' } },
  lift:  { machine: '5-mainlift-1', safe: { how: 'turn', at: '5-lift-brake', ok: v =&gt; v &gt;= 3 },
           clean: { how: 'hold', at: 'the car's door on the next deck', mins: 2 }, fix: { service: '5-mainlift-1' } },
  alarm: { machine: '3-galleyplant-1', safe: { how: 'hold', at: '3-galleyplant-alarm', mins: 1 },
           clean: { how: 'wait', at: '3-vent-1', mins: 5 }, fix: { look: hood, then service } } }</div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>The week's plan:</b> <code>incidentPlan(week)</code>: for weeks from Day 8's, a weekday (Mon-Fri, a <code>playerShiftOn</code> day, not an <code>eventsOn</code> event day, never the day of a test job or promotion) and a minute 540-930 from <code>schedU(week, 0, 870)</code>; the kind weighted by its machines' wear, picked with <code>schedU(week, 0, 871)</code>; the place with 872. Day 8's is fixed (burst, Deck 4, 630). If the day turns out a tradition evening's day, the incident is in the morning (before 12:00) so it's long over. Saved once planned.</li>
    <li><b>The job:</b> a job kind <code>incident</code> (urgency 2, held for you 30 minutes if you're on shift and on the ship, then the crew: two Works crew walk the three steps in 25-40 minutes), stops = safe, clean (repeated), then the fix job is posted as an ordinary repair held for you for the rest of the shift.</li>
    <li><b>Wrong valve:</b> nothing breaks; the water keeps coming ("Still running. That one's downstream.") and you pick again. Wrong brake direction: the turn just goes the other way.</li>
    <li><b>At night</b> only on your night shifts (Step 5 adds them); otherwise never 21:00-06:00.</li>
    <li><b>Notes:</b> <code>simNote('incident', { id, step: 'start' | 'safe' | 'clean' | 'fixed', by })</code>; reputation: first on the scene +2.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="save" class="builder">
  <h2>Save</h2>
  <ul><li><code>ship.works.inc = { plan: { [week]: [kind, day, minute, deck] }, open: null | { id, step, started } }</code>; the fix job in <code>ship.jobs</code>. Old plans (weeks before this one) dropped.</li></ul>
</section>

<section id="tests" class="builder">
  <h2>Tests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b><code>mech_check</code></b> (24f): each incident's three steps in order; a wrong valve doesn't end it; crew handle it when you don't come; never on an event day, a tradition evening, a day off, at night or before Day 8; Day 8's is a burst pipe at 10:30 on Deck 4; about one a week over 4 weeks; the same twice.</li>
    <li><b><code>day_check</code></b> on an incident day: everyone still reaches their places (the wet patch only re-routes; the stuck person is released); draw calls under 450 with the puddle and smoke.</li>
    <li><b><code>deck_check</code></b>: the new places reachable.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="ranges" class="builder">
  <h2>Builds and keys</h2>
  <ul><li>Seat <b>M2</b>, <code>claude/mech-incidents</code>, <b>0.51.x</b>. Hash keys <b>870-873</b> (870 the day and minute, 871 the kind, 872 the place, 873 the stuck person if two are riding).</li>
  <li><b>The stuck lift (the lead's call):</b> the builder takes the fallback unless the social engineer (sim on call) says holding a rider is cheap. The fallback, if holding a rider is costly: the lift incident ships without a rider (the lift just stalls, slow rides) and the "help them out" step becomes "check the car".</li></ul>
</section>

<section id="faq">
  <h2>Builders' questions</h2>
  <h3>Two ids (seat A, through the lead, 2026-10-18)</h3>
  <p><b>The lift machine:</b> <code>5-lift-1</code> is both a <code>lift-wait</code> place on Deck 5 and section 17's stand-in id for the main lift (<code>STUB_MACHINES[5]</code>). The machine is renamed <b><code>5-mainlift-1</code></b> (seat S, in <code>STUB_MACHINES</code>); <code>machinesLoad</code> reads an old save's <code>5-lift-1</code> entry as <code>5-mainlift-1</code>, so the lift keeps its wear; open jobs with the old id are dropped (re-posted next hour). The place keeps <code>5-lift-1</code>.</p>
  <p><b>The galley alarm:</b> there's no <code>3-extractor-1</code> in the game (its stand-in dropped out when the galley plant <code>3-galleyplant-1</code>, room <code>g</code>, was built). The alarm incident uses <code>3-galleyplant-1</code> and the place <code>3-galleyplant-alarm</code>.</p>
  <p><b>Seat A's branch</b> is <code>claude/deck-0607</code>.</p>
</section>
